{
 "fps": 30,
 "lead": 0.8,
 "tail": 2.0,
 "footer": "Sources: canada.ca \u00b7 CRA Canada child benefit: how much you can get (July 2026 \u2013 June 2027), T4114 \u00b7 T4127 (2026) \u00b7 Examples, general info, not advice",
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "L1",
   "file": "vo/L1.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Sara earns seventy thousand dollars. She has one child, under six. This year, her family gets five thousand, nine hundred and thirty-four dollars of Canada child benefit."
  },
  {
   "id": "L2",
   "file": "vo/L2.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "With one change on her tax return, the same family could get six thousand, six hundred and thirty-four. And pay less tax too."
  },
  {
   "id": "L3",
   "file": "vo/L3.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Altogether, about three thousand, six hundred and sixty-five dollars more in one year. Same job. Same child. Same income."
  },
  {
   "id": "L4",
   "file": "vo/L4.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "By the end of this video, you'll know exactly how the C C B is calculated, and the legal moves that change it."
  },
  {
   "id": "L5",
   "file": "vo/L5.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "All numbers: the C C B year from July twenty twenty-six to June twenty twenty-seven, Ontario taxes, twenty twenty-six rates. Examples, not real people. General information, not advice."
  },
  {
   "id": "L6",
   "file": "vo/L6.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "First: how the C C B is calculated."
  },
  {
   "id": "L7",
   "file": "vo/L7.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "The Canada child benefit is a tax-free monthly payment for families with children under eighteen."
  },
  {
   "id": "L8",
   "file": "vo/L8.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For July twenty twenty-six to June twenty twenty-seven, the maximum is eight thousand, one hundred and fifty-seven dollars a year for each child under six. That's six hundred and seventy-nine dollars and seventy-five cents a month."
  },
  {
   "id": "L9",
   "file": "vo/L9.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For a child aged six to seventeen, the maximum is six thousand, eight hundred and eighty-three."
  },
  {
   "id": "L10",
   "file": "vo/L10.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "But most families don't get the maximum. The amount shrinks as your income rises."
  },
  {
   "id": "L11",
   "file": "vo/L11.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And here's the key. It's not your salary that counts. It's your adjusted family net income, from your tax returns for the year before."
  },
  {
   "id": "L12",
   "file": "vo/L12.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For this benefit year, that's your twenty twenty-five income."
  },
  {
   "id": "L13",
   "file": "vo/L13.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the reduction."
  },
  {
   "id": "L14",
   "file": "vo/L14.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Once adjusted family net income passes thirty-eight thousand, two hundred and thirty-seven dollars, the benefit starts to drop."
  },
  {
   "id": "L15",
   "file": "vo/L15.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "With one child, it drops by seven percent of every dollar above that line, up to eighty-two thousand, eight hundred and forty-seven."
  },
  {
   "id": "L16",
   "file": "vo/L16.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "With three children, it drops by nineteen percent."
  },
  {
   "id": "L17",
   "file": "vo/L17.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "For Sara, at seventy thousand, that's seven percent of thirty-one thousand, seven hundred and sixty-three. A reduction of about two thousand, two hundred and twenty-three dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L18",
   "file": "vo/L18.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Eight thousand, one hundred and fifty-seven, minus that reduction: five thousand, nine hundred and thirty-four dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L19",
   "file": "vo/L19.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So every extra thousand dollars of net income costs Sara seventy dollars of C C B. And the reverse is also true."
  },
  {
   "id": "L20",
   "file": "vo/L20.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Every thousand dollars you take off your net income gives seventy dollars back. With three children, a hundred and ninety."
  },
  {
   "id": "L21",
   "file": "vo/L21.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Now, the move. Lever one: the R R S P."
  },
  {
   "id": "L22",
   "file": "vo/L22.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "An R R S P contribution is a deduction. It lowers your net income, and that's exactly the number the C C B uses."
  },
  {
   "id": "L23",
   "file": "vo/L23.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Say Sara contributes ten thousand dollars to her R R S P, and she has the room."
  },
  {
   "id": "L24",
   "file": "vo/L24.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Her net income drops to sixty thousand. Her C C B rises to six thousand, six hundred and thirty-four. Seven hundred dollars more."
  },
  {
   "id": "L25",
   "file": "vo/L25.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "And her income tax drops by about two thousand, nine hundred and sixty-five dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "L26",
   "file": "vo/L26.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Together: about three thousand, six hundred and sixty-five dollars from one ten-thousand-dollar contribution. And the ten thousand is still hers, in the R R S P."
  },
  {
   "id": "L27",
   "file": "vo/L27.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "But here's the timing most families miss. The C C B looks back."
  },
  {
   "id": "L28",
   "file": "vo/L28.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "A contribution for twenty twenty-six lowers your twenty twenty-six net income. That changes the C C B paid from July twenty twenty-seven."
  },
  {
   "id": "L29",
   "file": "vo/L29.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "So the benefit arrives the following year. And the thresholds are updated every July, so the exact numbers move a little."
  },
  {
   "id": "L30",
   "file": "vo/L30.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "With three children in the same income range, the same ten thousand dollars would add about one thousand, nine hundred of C C B, plus the tax saving."
  },
  {
   "id": "L31",
   "file": "vo/L31.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Lever two: other deductions. Child care expenses, union dues, and other deductions also lower net income. Claim every one you're entitled to."
  },
  {
   "id": "L32",
   "file": "vo/L32.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Lever three: file, every year, both of you. The C C B is calculated from both partners' returns."
  },
  {
   "id": "L33",
   "file": "vo/L33.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "If one return is missing, the C R A can't calculate the benefit, and payments can stop. Even with no income, file."
  },
  {
   "id": "L34",
   "file": "vo/L34.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Lever four: keep your information current. A new child, a separation, a move, or a change in custody can all change the amount. Tell the C R A when it happens."
  },
  {
   "id": "L35",
   "file": "vo/L35.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Where this changes. Provinces add their own child benefits, with their own rules. Above eighty-two thousand, eight hundred and forty-seven, the reduction rate changes. And a child with a disability may qualify for an extra benefit."
  },
  {
   "id": "L36",
   "file": "vo/L36.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Your exact amount comes from the C R A's calculation, so check it in My Account."
  },
  {
   "id": "L37",
   "file": "vo/L37.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "Here's your checklist."
  },
  {
   "id": "L38",
   "file": "vo/L38.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. Find your adjusted family net income from last year's returns."
  },
  {
   "id": "L39",
   "file": "vo/L39.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. If it's between thirty-eight thousand, two hundred and thirty-seven and eighty-two thousand, eight hundred and forty-seven, every deduction also raises your C C B."
  },
  {
   "id": "L40",
   "file": "vo/L40.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. Use your R R S P room, and claim child care and other deductions."
  },
  {
   "id": "L41",
   "file": "vo/L41.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Four. Both partners file on time, every year."
  },
  {
   "id": "L42",
   "file": "vo/L42.mp3",
   "gap": 1.0,
   "text": "So, what did we learn?"
  },
  {
   "id": "L43",
   "file": "vo/L43.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "One. The C C B uses net income, not salary."
  },
  {
   "id": "L44",
   "file": "vo/L44.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Two. Each dollar of deduction can come back twice: less tax, and more benefit."
  },
  {
   "id": "L45",
   "file": "vo/L45.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Three. The benefit arrives the following July."
  },
  {
   "id": "L46",
   "file": "vo/L46.mp3",
   "gap": 0.35,
   "text": "Next on this channel: tax credits versus tax deductions, and why the same thousand dollars can be worth very different amounts. Subscribe, so you don't miss it."
  }
 ],
